fastjj embeds modified jj-cli and jj-lib 0.37.0 by The Jujutsu Authors,
under Apache-2.0. Upstream: https://github.com/jj-vcs/jj/tree/v0.37.0
(commit 11c3dbe17ac0a2172755789613fa8f04a50118a0).

The vendored crates come from the published crates.io packages, retaining
upstream copyright and license notices. The CLI adds in-memory arguments and
configuration, native text editing and credential callbacks, and removes
standalone binary/test declarations from its manifest. jj-lib replaces the Git
subprocess transport with native libgit2 fetch, push leases, remote discovery,
refspec exclusions and pruning. Repository storage remains the jj 0.37 format.
fastjj supplies native libssh2 transport, SSH config/key/agent support,
thread-based jump tunnels, and kernel process restrictions.

fastjjui embeds modified jjui 0.10.11 by ibrahim dursun and contributors, under
MIT. Upstream: https://github.com/idursun/jjui/tree/v0.10.11
(commit cd1da156b1d4d4cae6bedd7fd1f1f23ca42f8f0e).
The license is retained in vendor/jjui/LICENSE and release licenses/jjui-MIT.txt.
The fork replaces backend argv and askpass subprocesses with inherited private
request/credential descriptors, uses the native editor, and blocks shell and
Lua process entry points. The UI retains the upstream module path for imports.
